# ---- HOST-NATIVE STATION (native from day one — domainos wave, 2026-09-09/10) ----
# Apollo DN3500 (MC68030, 25 MHz, 16 MB, 8-plane colour) running Domain/OS
# SR10.4.1 — the Display Manager desktop. MAME's dn3500 driver (src/mame/
# apollo/apollo.cpp) runs ON THE HOST: drawshm frames, ctlsock keys through the
# generated keymap, no audio plane (the DM is silent).
# Launcher: shared stations/mame-native/x11-runtime.sh.
#
# THIS STATION IS PINNED TO MAME 0.276, NOT THE FLEET'S 0.289. Do not "fix"
# the deviation: on 0.289 every Normal-mode boot of this machine is black
# forever with all four front-panel LEDs lit — the boot ROM's KEYBOARD
# self-test spins at PC 0x67a2-0x67b2 polling the SIO. Service mode works on
# 0.289 because it skips the self-tests, which is what makes the asymmetry
# look like a disk problem. The pin lives in native.d/domainos.sh
# (NATIVE_MAME_TAG=mame0276); see docs/lab/DOMAINOS-WAVE.md wall 1.
SH_RESET_MODE=relaunch
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=Apollo DN3500 Domain/OS SR10.4.1 Display Manager desktop, logged in as user: three overlapping pads — pad0000 with a /com/ld / listing of the Domain/OS root (bsd4.3 and sys5.3 side by side) and a /com/lcnode node table (node 2616D, entry directory //mess), pad0001 an empty shell pad, pad0002 the process display (init, display_manager, rgyd, lcpd, glbd, mbx_helper) — over the DM's Command: bar.
MAME_NATIVE_BIN=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/domainos/mame-native/domainos
MAME_NATIVE_DRIVER=dn3500
MAME_NATIVE_ROMS=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/domainos/mame-native/roms
MAME_NATIVE_GEOM=1024x768
# The 3C505 card's 3c505-nw.bin has NO GOOD DUMP KNOWN, so every start raises
# MAME's startup warning panel — and that panel PAUSES the machine until a key
# is pressed, which a headless kiosk never sends. skip_warnings is only
# honoured with the skip-warnings patch (atari800xl's finding), which this
# station's binary carries.
MAME_NATIVE_SKIP_WARNINGS=1
MAME_NATIVE_CHECKPOINT=1
# ...but the RESET takes the service-restart path, not the fleet's fast
# in-process LOADST. MEASURED 2026-09-10 on the baked golden: an in-process
# LOADST restores the machine correctly (the emulated clock rewinds, the guest
# forgets a window opened after the save — proven by asking it: a fresh
# `cp /com/pst` came back numbered pad0003 again with pad0002 gone) and yet
# leaves the PREVIOUS VISITOR'S PIXELS on the glass, because apollo_v.cpp
# repaints the screen from its image memory only when m_update_flag is set and
# a restore brings that flag back as it was. A fresh process starts with a
# blank framebuffer and paints the restored state in full — proven by
# relaunching with -state golden. ~16 s instead of ~0.4 s; correctness wins.
SH_MAME_RESET_INPROCESS=0
# -view: MEASURED 2026-09-09 — the driver's DEFAULT view snapshots at 1024x844
# (the raster plus a strip of function-key legends and LEDs, a MAME artefact,
# not the machine), and the layout's own "XGA Screen (1024x768)" name is NOT
# honoured by the drawshm target. "Screen 0 Standard (4:3)" is the bare raster
# at the fleet geometry and is the only name that works here.
# -disk1 is the POST-CALENDAR disk, not the pristine media. The pristine image
# halts in the boot ROM ("More than 14 days have elapsed since the last
# shutdown... run CALENDAR") and no RTC trick satisfies it; the disk is
# composed by booting it ONCE in Service mode and answering CALENDAR
# (tiles/domainos.sh). NEVER point this at media/domainos.awd.
# The disk is a FRESH COPY of the immutable golden image on every start (see
# MAME_NATIVE_DISK_TEMPLATE below): MAME writes an .awd in place, the service
# stops by SIGKILL because this binary ignores SIGTERM, and a checkpoint is
# only valid against the bytes its disk had when it was saved. MEASURED
# 2026-09-10: without this the station restored the golden against a drifted
# disk, the guest declared its boot volume inconsistent and cold-booted into
# SALVAGING BOOT VOL, which rewrote the disk again on every start.
MAME_NATIVE_DISK_TEMPLATE=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/domainos/media/domainos-station.awd:disk.awd
MAME_NATIVE_ARGS=-isa1 wdc -isa2 ctape -isa3 3c505 -view "Screen 0 Standard (4:3)" -disk1 /data/vms/streamhost/stations/domainos/disk.awd
SH_MAMECTL_SOCK=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/domainos/ctl.sock
SH_MAMESOCK_KEYMAP=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/domainos/domainos.keymap
# ---- POINTER: NONE, and the reason is proven, not suspected ----
# The Apollo 3-button mouse hangs off the keyboard (apollo_kbd.cpp), and
# apple2e's whole open-loop stack is compiled in and correctly configured
# below — the module applies every count (STAT: applied=660,300). Nothing
# moves, because apollo_kbd's kbd_scan_timer() calls read_mouse() ONLY when
# m_mode != KBD_MODE_0_COMPATIBILITY, and a gdb dprintf on
# apollo_kbd_device::set_mode recorded ZERO hits across a full boot, login and
# count burst (2026-09-10): the emulated keyboard never leaves compatibility
# mode, so the mouse ports are never sampled. Domain/OS would have to send the
# keyboard the bytes 0xFF 0x01 to reach KBD_MODE_1_KEYSTATE (read_mouse then
# self-promotes to KBD_MODE_2 on the first motion); the DM's own pointer init
# is the likely trigger and never runs on this disk — it prints
# "(CMDF) user_data/startup_dm.191 - name not found" on every boot.
# The settings stay so the next attempt starts from a configured engine.
MAME_CTL_PTR_TAGS=:kbd:mouse1,:kbd:mouse2,:kbd:mouse3
MAME_CTL_BTN_NAMES=Left mouse button,Right mouse button,Center mouse button
MAME_CTL_PTR_MOD=256
MAME_CTL_SCREEN=1024x768
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=60
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PIDFILE=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/domainos/mame.pid
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PROC_MATCH=assets/domainos/mame-native
MAME_NATIVE_STANDBY_DELAY_S=8
# ---- KEYBOARD: 180 ms per EDGE, MEASURED ----
# The Apollo keyboard is a 1200-baud serial device, not a CPU-scanned matrix,
# so MAME_CTL_KEY_EXCL does NOT apply. But the fleet floor of 80/80 leaks the
# Shift key by exactly one character: at 80 ms per edge
# "echo Apollo DN3500 Domain/OS SR10.4.1" arrived on the framebuffer as
# "APollo dN#500 - dOmain/Os sr!0.4.1" — every shifted character one key late.
# At ~180 ms per edge the same line typed byte-perfect, twice (2026-09-10).
# The launcher maps these onto MAME_CTL_KEY_HOLD/GAP.
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=180
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=180
